1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:07,078
The oldest city in America, and a beach you can drive on!

2
00:00:07,078 --> 00:00:10,047
A Spanish fort you reach by a free ferry.

3
00:00:10,047 --> 00:00:12,147
The world's first oceanarium.

4
00:00:12,147 --> 00:00:14,030
And Daytona's famous sand!

5
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:15,784
This is St.

6
00:00:15,784 --> 00:00:21,701
Augustine to Daytona Beach on Scenic A1A: about 60 miles down the Atlantic coast.

7
00:00:21,701 --> 00:00:25,500
Stick around till the end for the full trip planner!

8
00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:27,574
Here's the plan!

9
00:00:27,574 --> 00:00:28,628
We start in St.

10
00:00:28,628 --> 00:00:35,090
Augustine, then Fort Matanzas, Marineland and Flagler Beach, and we finish in Daytona Beach!

11
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:37,635
We're starting in St.

12
00:00:37,635 --> 00:00:40,369
Augustine, founded way back in 1565!

13
00:00:40,369 --> 00:00:45,837
Walk the stone walls of the Castillo de San Marcos, then wander down St.

14
00:00:45,837 --> 00:00:46,900
George Street.

15
00:00:47,850 --> 00:00:51,850
Over the Bridge of Lions, then south on A1A, right along the dunes!

16
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:54,275
This is Fort Matanzas!

17
00:00:54,275 --> 00:01:00,375
Hop on the free ferry across the river to a little Spanish fort, built in 1742 to guard St.

18
00:01:00,375 --> 00:01:01,850
Augustine's back door.

19
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:05,920
Just a few miles down A1A to a Florida legend!

20
00:01:06,870 --> 00:01:08,436
Welcome to Marineland!

21
00:01:08,436 --> 00:01:14,343
It opened in 1938 as the world's first oceanarium, built to film movies underwater.

22
00:01:14,343 --> 00:01:16,620
Today you can meet the dolphins!

23
00:01:17,570 --> 00:01:23,570
Now A1A runs right along the ocean, with the dunes on one side and the beach just over them!

24
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:26,234
Welcome to Flagler Beach!

25
00:01:26,234 --> 00:01:30,829
Walk out on the fishing pier, and check out the orange-tinted sand.

26
00:01:30,829 --> 00:01:33,640
It's full of tiny crushed coquina shells!

27
00:01:34,590 --> 00:01:39,760
Through Ormond Beach, where car racing on the sand began, and on to Daytona!

28
00:01:40,710 --> 00:01:44,540
We made it to Daytona Beach, the World's Most Famous Beach!

29
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:49,408
You can drive right on the sand here, nice and slow, at ten miles per hour.

30
00:01:49,408 --> 00:01:51,420
Then head over to the Speedway!

31
00:01:52,370 --> 00:01:53,829
And that's the drive!

32
00:01:53,829 --> 00:01:59,250
About 60 miles from the nation's oldest city to the World's Most Famous Beach.

33
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:03,360
Here's your trip planner, everything in one place.

34
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:05,130
Pause and grab a screenshot!

35
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:10,231
Thanks for riding along!

36
00:02:10,231 --> 00:02:18,270
Subscribe to Road Trip Atlas for more Florida road trips, and next time we're heading to the Panhandle for Scenic Highway 30A!
